  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing API Routes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the backend API route handlers. I\'ve started defining the routes in `src/server/routes/auth.ts`. I plan to implement POST requests for `/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/register`, and a `/api/auth/switch-` route. The login route will validate credentials or offer a demo quick-switch option. The register route will create new users and send a notification.\n\n\n**Defining More Routes**\n\nI\'ve expanded the API route definitions considerably. I\'m adding routes for user profile management with `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/profile`.  Then, I\'m working on routes for catalog data retrieval (`/api/catalog`), bookings management (`/api/bookings`), and queue functionalities using SSE (`/api/queue/stream`). The bookings routes include draft creation, cancellation, and retrieval options.\n\n\n**Expanding Route Definitions**\n\nI\'m now detailing more of the backend API routes. I\'ve focused on payment integration, crafting routes for order creation, verification (including signature validation), and webhook handling for Razorpay or test order simulations. I\'m also putting in work on interviewer-related endpoints, including application submission, status retrieval, availability toggling, earnings tracking, and payout requests. Furthermore, I\'ve outlined routes for feedback submission, review processes, and dispute resolution mechanisms.\n\n\n**Defining Admin Routes**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining the admin routes. I\'ve outlined endpoints for platform metrics, user management (listing, filtering, status updates), and handling interviewer applications (evaluation, approval, rejection). I\'m also including tier management, round template creation, and an immutable accounting ledger. Furthermore, I\'ve added refund review and resolution mechanisms, audit logs, and settings management (listing and updates) in my admin definitions. Finally, I\'m defining notification routes for fetching and marking as read.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1204979"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import { Router } from \'express\';\\nimport { store } from \'../store\';\\nimport { UserRole } from \'../../types\';\\n\\nexport const authRouter = Router();\\n\\n// Get current session user\\nauthRouter.get(\'/me\', (req, res) => {\\n  const userId = (req.headers[\'x-user-id\'] as string) || \'usr_candidate_1\';\\n  const user = store.users.get(userId);\\n  if (!user) {\\n    return res.status(401).json({ error: \'User not found\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  const candidateProfile = store.candidateProfiles.get(userId);\\n  const interviewerProfile = store.interviewerProfiles.get(userId);\\n\\n  return res.json({\\n    user: {\\n      ...user,\\n      candidateProfile,\\n      interviewerProfile,\\n    },\\n  });\\n});\\n\\n// Quick switch between demo seed users for easy testing of Candidate, Interviewer, and Admin perspectives\\nauthRouter.post(\'/switch-user\', (req, res) => {\\n  const { userId } = req.body;\\n  const user = store.users.get(userId);\\n  if (!user) {\\n    return res.status(404).json({ error: \'User not found\' });\\n  }\\n  return res.json({ success: true, user });\\n});\\n\\n// Switch active role for current user\\nauthRouter.post(\'/switch-role\', (req, res) => {\\n  const userId = (req.headers[\'x-user-id\'] as string) || \'usr_candidate_1\';\\n  const { role } = req.body as { role: UserRole };\\n\\n  const user = store.users.get(userId);\\n  if (!user) {\\n    return res.status(404).json({ error: \'User not found\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!user.roles.includes(role)) {\\n    // If user wants to switch to interviewer, check if profile exists, or grant candidate\\n    user.roles.push(role);\\n  }\\n\\n  user.activeRole = role;\\n  return res.json({ success: true, user });\\n});\\n\\n// Login\\nauthRouter.post(\'/login\', (req, res) => {\\n  const { email } = req.body;\\n  if (!email) {\\n    return res.status(400).json({ error: \'Email is required\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  const existing = Array.from(store.users.values()).find(\\n    (u) => u.email.toLowerCase() === String(email).toLowerCase()\\n  );\\n\\n  if (!existing) {\\n    return res.status(401).json({ error: \'Invalid credentials. Try deepanshu.chawla2608@gmail.com, sarah.lead@interviewer.com, or admin@interviewarena.com\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (existing.isSuspended) {\\n    return res.status(403).json({ error: \'Account suspended. Contact administrator.\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  return res.json({ success: true, user: existing });\\n});\\n\\n// Register\\nauthRouter.post(\'/register\', (req, res) => {\\n  const { email, fullName, role = \'CANDIDATE\' } = req.body;\\n  if (!email || !fullName) {\\n    return res.status(400).json({ error: \'Email and full name are required\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  const existing = Array.from(store.users.values()).find(\\n    (u) => u.email.toLowerCase() === String(email).toLowerCase()\\n  );\\n  if (existing) {\\n    return res.status(409).json({ error: \'User with this email already exists\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  const newId = \'usr_\' + Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 9);\\n  const newUser = {\\n    id: newId,\\n    email,\\n    fullName,\\n    roles: [role as UserRole],\\n    activeRole: role as UserRole,\\n    isSuspended: false,\\n    emailVerified: true,\\n    createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\\n  };\\n\\n  store.users.set(newId, newUser);\\n\\n  if (role === \'CANDIDATE\') {\\n    store.candidateProfiles.set(newId, {\\n      id: \'prof_\' + newId,\\n      userId: newId,\\n      targetRoles: [\'Software Engineer\'],\\n      experienceLevel: \'STUDENT\',\\n      preferredLanguages: [\'Python\', \'JavaScript\'],\\n      timezone: \'Asia/Kolkata\',\\n      totalSessions: 0,\\n      totalSpent: 0,\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  store.addNotification(\\n    newId,\\n    \'Welcome to Interview Arena!\',\\n    \'Your account is ready. Explore Tier A, B, and C practice tracks to supercharge your interview preparation.\',\\n    \'SUCCESS\'\\n  );\\n\\n  return res.status(201).json({ success: true, user: newUser });\\n});\\n\\n// Update Profile\\nauthRouter.post(\'/profile\', (req, res) => {\\n  const userId = (req.headers[\'x-user-id\'] as string) || \'usr_candidate_1\';\\n  const { fullName, bio, targetRoles, experienceLevel, preferredLanguages, graduationYear, collegeOrEmployer } = req.body;\\n\\n  const user = store.users.get(userId);\\n  if (!user) {\\n    return res.status(404).json({ error: \'User not found\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (fullName) user.fullName = fullName;\\n\\n  let candProfile = store.candidateProfiles.get(userId);\\n  if (!candProfile) {\\n    candProfile = {\\n      id: \'prof_\' + userId,\\n      userId,\\n      targetRoles: targetRoles || [\'Software Engineer\'],\\n      experienceLevel: experienceLevel || \'STUDENT\',\\n      preferredLanguages: preferredLanguages || [\'Python\'],\\n      timezone: \'Asia/Kolkata\',\\n      totalSessions: 0,\\n      totalSpent: 0,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (bio !== undefined) candProfile.bio = bio;\\n  if (targetRoles) candProfile.targetRoles = targetRoles;\\n  if (experienceLevel) candProfile.experienceLevel = experienceLevel;\\n  if (preferredLanguages) candProfile.preferredLanguages = preferredLanguages;\\n  if (graduationYear) candProfile.graduationYear = Number(graduationYear);\\n  if (collegeOrEmployer) candProfile.collegeOrEmployer = collegeOrEmployer;\\n\\n  store.candidateProfiles.set(userId, candProfile);\\n\\n  return res.json({ success: true, user, candidateProfile: candProfile });\\n});\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create auth router with multi-role switching, login, registration, and profile updates\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/server/routes/auth.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing file\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create auth routes\"}"
