  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Integrating MongoDB Functionality**\n\nI\'m now completely focused on MongoDB integration. My primary task is building out the complete schema and integrating either Mongoose or the native MongoDB driver. This includes defining collections, schemas, setting up the connection, and creating essential seed scripts. The plan is to ensure seamless data management from the start.\n\n\n**Implementing MongoDB and UPI**\n\nI\'ve made significant strides in integrating MongoDB. I\'ve defined comprehensive schemas for critical entities like Users, CandidateProfiles, and Payments. Configuration for MongoDB is also complete in `.env.example`, `docker-compose.yml`, and documentation is prepared. My next move is adapting the backend data layer to seamlessly use MongoDB when `MONGODB_URI` is available, maintaining the transactional in-memory fallback for development. Now, I\'m integrating direct UPI payment workflows to support both Checkout and Payouts.\n\n\n**Developing In-house Features**\n\nI\'m now deep in building internal features. I\'m prioritizing the in-house video meeting solution; it will have WebRTC, screen sharing, live chat, and a collaborative canvas. The aim is a seamless experience within the workspace. Concurrently, I\'m working on the light and dark theme toggle. I\'m focusing on persistent state management in local storage and a clean, contrasting design.\n\n\n"
