  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering MongoDB Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on integrating MongoDB. I\'m building a robust MongoDB client connection manager with auto-reconnect, indexing capabilities, and pre-defined collection references, like `usersCollection` and `candidateProfilesCollection`, in `src/db/mongodb.ts`.\n\n\n**Expanding MongoDB References**\n\nI\'ve extended the MongoDB collection references to include crucial collections like `interviewerProfilesCollection`, `interviewerApplicationsCollection`, `tiersCollection`, and many others, which cover core business logic. I also devised a seed function to populate MongoDB with default tiers, company tracks, round curricula, and demo users. It gracefully defaults to an in-memory transactional store for resilience in the face of connectivity issues. I\'m updating documentation and configuration files to reflect these changes.\n\n\n**Prioritizing UPI Payment Flows**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on deep UPI integration as the primary payment method for the platform in India. I\'m exploring generating standard UPI URIs, rendering interactive QR codes using the `qrcode` library, and providing one-click launch buttons for popular UPI apps (Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm, BHIM). I\'m also including a \"Copy UPI ID\" option and a direct UPI Collect Request form for a seamless user experience. Finally, I\'m integrating UTR/Transaction Reference verification.\n\n\n**Designing In-House Arena**\n\nI\'m now designing an in-house meeting room, \"Arena Meet,\" directly within the Session Workspace, a move away from external tools. It will feature live WebRTC camera and mic feeds with a robust fallback. I\'m implementing mute/unmute toggles, camera controls with avatars, and screen sharing capabilities. Dual-participant views, an in-house live chat, and a collaborative code runner/whiteboard are also in the works.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1717928"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\n\\ntype Theme = \'light\' | \'dark\';\\n\\ninterface ThemeContextType {\\n  theme: Theme;\\n  toggleTheme: () => void;\\n  setTheme: (theme: Theme) => void;\\n}\\n\\nconst ThemeContext = createContext<ThemeContextType | undefined>(undefined);\\n\\nexport const ThemeProvider: React.FC<{ children: React.ReactNode }> = ({ children }) => {\\n  const [theme, setThemeState] = useState<Theme>(() => {\\n    const saved = localStorage.getItem(\'ia_theme\');\\n    if (saved === \'light\' || saved === \'dark\') return saved;\\n    return \'dark\'; // default theme\\n  });\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    localStorage.setItem(\'ia_theme\', theme);\\n    const root = document.documentElement;\\n    if (theme === \'dark\') {\\n      root.classList.add(\'dark\');\\n      root.classList.remove(\'light\');\\n      document.body.style.backgroundColor = \'#020617\';\\n      document.body.style.color = \'#f8fafc\';\\n    } else {\\n      root.classList.add(\'light\');\\n      root.classList.remove(\'dark\');\\n      document.body.style.backgroundColor = \'#f8fafc\';\\n      document.body.style.color = \'#0f172a\';\\n    }\\n  }, [theme]);\\n\\n  const toggleTheme = () => {\\n    setThemeState((prev) => (prev === \'dark\' ? \'light\' : \'dark\'));\\n  };\\n\\n  const setTheme = (t: Theme) => {\\n    setThemeState(t);\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <ThemeContext.Provider value={{ theme, toggleTheme, setTheme }}>\\n      {children}\\n    </ThemeContext.Provider>\\n  );\\n};\\n\\nexport const useTheme = () => {\\n  const context = useContext(ThemeContext);\\n  if (!context) {\\n    throw new Error(\'useTheme must be used within a ThemeProvider\');\\n  }\\n  return context;\\n};\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create ThemeContext with light and dark mode toggling and persistence\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/context/ThemeContext.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing file\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create ThemeContext\"}"
