  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request**: Build **Interview Arena**, a full-stack mock interview marketplace and live practice application with Tier A (\342\202\271100), Tier B (\342\202\27180), and Tier C (\342\202\27160) company preparation tracks, configurable rounds, real-time matchmaking queue with atomic claiming, financial ledger (20% platform commission, 80% interviewer share), 2-stage interviewer screening pipeline, in-house video meeting solution (embedded WebRTC, chat, code runner), direct UPI payment integration (dynamic scannable QR, UPI app intents, VPA collect, UTR verification), MongoDB integration with Docker Compose, and persistent Light/Dark theme switching.\n- **Constraints & Boundaries**:\n  - No `window.alert` / `window.confirm` / `window.open` (violates iFrame constraints; all replaced with in-app state/modals).\n  - Dev server runs on port 3000 via `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"`.\n  - No 3rd-party meeting redirects: all video meetings run via embedded in-house conference room.\n  - Transparent pricing: server strictly validates price from tier configurations.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Backend & Database**:\n  - `server.ts`: Express backend mounting Vite middlewares in dev, serving REST API routes and Server-Sent Events (`/api/queue/stream`).\n  - `src/db/mongodb.ts`: MongoDB client connection manager with auto-reconnect, collection accessors, and index setup (`users`, `bookings`, `queue_entries`, `ledger`, `tiers`).\n  - `src/server/store.ts`: ACID in-memory transactional store with row-level mutex lock (`claimQueueEntryAtomic`), pre-seeded with 4 test personas and initial data.\n  - `src/server/routes/`: `auth.ts`, `catalog.ts`, `bookings.ts`, `queue.ts`, `payments.ts`, `interviewer.ts`, `feedback.ts`, `admin.ts`, `notifications.ts`.\n  - `docker-compose.yml`: Configured with `mongo:7.0`, Mongo Express GUI (`:8081`), and web applet.\n  - `migrations/0001_initial_schema.sql`: Complete PostgreSQL schema preserved for relational deployments.\n- **Frontend & Components**:\n  - `src/context/ThemeContext.tsx`: Global Light/Dark mode context with `localStorage` persistence and body class toggling.\n  - `src/components/Navbar.tsx`: Persona quick-switcher, role switcher (`CANDIDATE`, `INTERVIEWER`, `ADMIN`), live queue badge, notifications dropdown, and Sun/Moon theme toggle.\n  - `src/components/CandidateDashboard.tsx`: Practice progress, active queue tracker card, recommended pathway selector, completed session reports.\n  - `src/components/CatalogView.tsx`: Tier filtering (A/B/C), company tracks (Google, Meta, Amazon, Microsoft, Uber, FinTech, Campus), round curriculum details, and booking modal trigger.\n  - `src/components/CheckoutModal.tsx`: Complete UPI integration (dynamic scannable QR code via `qrcode`, GPay/PhonePe/Paytm/BHIM intents, VPA collect request, UTR verification) and card fallback.\n  - `src/components/InHouseMeetingRoom.tsx`: Built-in WebRTC conference room (camera/mic feeds, screen share, mute/video toggles, live in-call chat, interactive code runner sandbox).\n  - `src/components/SessionWorkspace.tsx`: Live workspace embedding `InHouseMeetingRoom`, countdown timer, checklist, private notes, and feedback submission.\n  - `src/components/QueueTrackerModal.tsx`: Real-time queue radar, position in line, estimated wait time, auto-match transition, and 100% instant refund button.\n  - `src/components/InterviewerDashboard.tsx`: Online/offline availability toggle, incoming queue radar, 1-click atomic claiming, earnings ledger, and payout withdrawal modal.\n  - `src/components/InterviewerApplication.tsx`: \"Become an Interviewer\" pipeline with Screening 1 & 2 progress and admin review.\n  - `src/components/FeedbackModal.tsx`: 5-point structured rubric scoring, strengths, improvement areas, readiness verdict.\n  - `src/components/ReviewModal.tsx`: Candidate 1\342\200\2235 star rating and comment.\n  - `src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`: Live database metrics, user management, screening review & approvals, tier pricing configuration, ledger audit, and dispute resolution.\n  - `src/components/PolicyModals.tsx` & `Footer.tsx`: Terms, 100% refund guarantee, privacy, FAQ, and legal disclaimers.\n- **Testing & Verification**:\n  - `tests/run-all.ts`: 6/6 tests passing (`npm test` exits 0: unit pricing, ledger balance, atomic mutex claim concurrency, qualification gating, full E2E workflow).\n  - `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit`): 0 errors.\n  - `compile_applet`: Succeeded.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Iframe Constraint**: Standard browser dialogs (`window.alert`, `window.confirm`, `window.prompt`) fail or block inside AI Studio\'s preview iframe. All user confirmations (e.g. queue cancellation, admin approvals) must use direct state/modals.\n- **Concurrency & Overlapping Protection**: `claimQueueEntryAtomic` must clear or mark completed previous test sessions before subsequent tests run for the same interviewer ID, as the system strictly blocks overlapping active sessions (`CLAIMED`, `IN_PROGRESS`).\n- **MongoDB Fallback**: `src/db/mongodb.ts` attempts connection to `MONGODB_URI` but seamlessly falls back to the in-memory transactional store with row-level locks when MongoDB daemon is not running in the local container, ensuring both standalone preview and Docker Compose work out of the box.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- **Dev Server**: Running on `http://0.0.0.0:3000` via `tsx server.ts`.\n- **Pre-seeded Personas** in `store.ts`:\n  - Candidate: `deepanshu.chawla2608@gmail.com` (`usr_candidate_1`)\n  - Approved Interviewer: `sarah.lead@interviewer.com` (`usr_interviewer_1`, Tier A/B/C qualified, active earnings)\n  - Applicant: `alex.dev@applicant.com` (`usr_applicant_1`, screening required)\n  - Admin: `admin@interviewarena.com` (`usr_admin_1`, full access)\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. Deliver the final response to the user summarizing:\n   - Full MongoDB connection setup (`src/db/mongodb.ts`) and `docker-compose.yml` (`mongo:7.0`).\n   - Deep UPI integration (dynamic QR, GPay/PhonePe/Paytm/BHIM intents, VPA collect, UTR confirmation).\n   - In-house video meeting room (`InHouseMeetingRoom.tsx`) with camera, mic, screen share, chat, and code sandbox.\n   - Light and dark theme toggle (`ThemeContext.tsx` and navbar switch).\n2. If further requested, wire MongoDB persistence directly to external replica sets or provide MongoDB Atlas connection instructions.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Built-in video meeting is completely in-house with zero 3rd-party external app redirects.\n- Payment flow features real UPI as the primary payment method.\n- No blocking browser dialogs (`window.alert`/`window.confirm`) remain in any component.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 291
    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
