  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Tailwind v4**\n\nI\'m now diving into Tailwind CSS v4\'s structure and implementation. I\'ve noted that the package is installed and `@import \"tailwindcss\";` is present in `src/index.css`. To implement the `.dark` class effectively, it requires `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));`. This seems to be a key element for the framework to manage dark mode customization.\n\n\n**Clarifying Dark Mode Dynamics**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the behavior of `dark:` prefixes in Tailwind v4. It appears using `dark:bg-slate-900` or `dark:text-white` doesn\'t inherently work with the `.dark` class, unless a `@custom-variant` is declared. I\'ve found this crucial, especially when looking at the original CSS. There are direct style overrides for light mode and the light mode overrides all the dark mode classes!\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1408395"
