  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Configuration Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `.env.example` file. It seems crucial for setting up the Google Calendar and Meet conference integration. The notes point towards Google Cloud Console, specifically the APIs & Services section, and emphasize the necessary scope for calendar events. This will be the foundational starting point for the project. The configuration file seems simple, but it is necessary for authentication and authorization.\n\n\n**Refining Configuration Guidelines**\n\nI\'ve decided to refine the `.env.example` file. I\'m removing the Google OAuth-related secrets entirely because our application utilizes an in-house WebRTC solution and doesn\'t require Google Meet or OAuth integration. I\'m also eliminating other potentially prompting API keys, like Razorpay and Resend. I will keep only necessary core configuration variables like the port, node environment, and application URL.\n\n\n"
