    thinking: "**Refining Video Options**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `AdminDashboard.tsx` file, specifically lines 349-366. I\'m considering refining the \"Google Meet / Video\" option to something more descriptive: \"In-House Video Meeting Room.\" I also want to highlight that this includes \"NATIVE WEBRTC ACTIVE\" with \"Embedded camera, audio, screen share, chat & code sandbox (no 3rd-party dependencies).\"\n\n\n**Analyzing Light Theme Issues**\n\nI\'m now investigating a light theme discrepancy. Some elements aren\'t rendering with the correct white theme colors. I\'ve started by examining `src/index.css` for light theme styling. I\'ll check each component\'s CSS to ensure consistent application of the light theme, starting with the root and header.\n\n\n**Addressing Light Theme Overrides**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a major problem in `src/index.css`. The rule `html.light .text-white { color: #0f172a !important; }` is overriding text color, which I now realize is causing significant issues for elements like buttons and badges. It\'s making the text invisible, and the `!important` declaration makes it a priority I hadn\'t realized. I\'m going to remove this section entirely, because it\'s breaking a lot of things.\n\n\n**Diagnosing Color Contrast Issues**\n\nI\'m now focusing on color contrast problems caused by the light theme. Several button and badge styles render poorly, such as indigo and emerald, because the text becomes dark and has low visibility on the background. I\'ve realized `text-indigo-300`, `text-emerald-300`, and `text-amber-300` are also causing similar issues. I\'m considering using contrasting color values, like switching to `text-indigo-700` in light mode to improve readability. I also need to evaluate similar issues for slate opacity variants.\n\n\n"
