    thinking: "**Analyzing Color Contrast**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the color contrast within `CandidateDashboard.tsx`, specifically line 78. The dark gradient and white text in the banner stood out. However, I need to reconcile this with the application\'s overall color scheme, especially the styles defined in `src/index.css`. This may require some refactoring or conditional styling to optimize for both light and dark modes.\n\n\n**Investigating Color Conflicts**\n\nI\'ve discovered a critical issue in `src/index.css` related to light mode. The CSS overrides all instances of `.text-white` to dark slate, rendering text on the indigo gradient banner and other elements unreadable. Furthermore, elements with `bg-indigo-600` and `bg-emerald-600` are affected as well, along with `bg-slate-900` classes, which has issues with opacity due to Tailwind\'s implementation. I need to figure out how to solve all these issues in a systematic way.\n\n\n"
