backgrounds, as in the previous light theme updates. I\'m using `:not()` pseudo-classes to exclude specific classes, such as background colors, to ensure text readability. I\'m making further adjustments to badge styling to improve the light theme\'s appearance.\n\n\n**Implementing Light Theme Colors**\n\nI\'ve added light theme overrides to `src/index.css` to handle specific text and background colors for improved contrast. I\'ve focused on re-defining indigo, emerald, amber, and rose tones to their darker counterparts, ensuring better readability and accessibility. I\'m especially happy with how clean and concise these overrides are, making it easier to maintain and extend the light theme\'s color palette.\n\n\n**Improving Theme Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on improving the aesthetics, starting with pill badges. I\'m excited to see them gain high contrast in the light theme, featuring pastel backgrounds and deep-toned text for clear readability. I\'ve also implemented light theme overrides to the cards and background colors, and the modal backdrop is now easily readable in light mode. I\'m focusing on ensuring these elements are accessible.\n\n\n**Refining Light Theme Overrides**\n\nI\'ve just added several light theme overrides to `src/index.css` to refine the appearance of input fields, text areas, and select elements, making them more readable. I\'m also considering light theme adjustments for video elements and meeting rooms such as the dark video feeds and participant boxes, and how they should be presented in the light theme. I\'m focusing on ensuring these elements are accessible and comfortable to view.\n\n\n"
