  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**: Implement real production-level login/logout authentication and authorization (RBAC) so that upon publishing, unauthorized users cannot freely view interviewer and admin screens. Remove dummy/mock data and store all application data (tracks, bookings, queue, reviews, ledger) in a real persistent database.\n   - **User Email**: `deepanshu.chawla2608@gmail.com` (designated super-admin).\n   - **Key Requirements**:\n     - Replace hardcoded demo persona switching with real Firebase Auth (Google Sign-In via popup).\n     - Persist real data to Firestore (remove static mock candidate/interviewer bookings).\n     - Strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC): Candidate, Interviewer (pending/approved verification), Admin (`deepanshu.chawla2608@gmail.com`). Unauthenticated users see public catalog/landing page and login prompt; candidates cannot see interviewer/admin portals; unverified interviewers cannot claim paid sessions; only admins can access the admin dashboard.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Previously Completed**:\n     - Built comprehensive mock interview platform (catalog tiers A/B/C: \342\202\271100/\342\202\27180/\342\202\27160, atomic claiming, WebRTC meeting room, rubric feedback, ledger).\n     - Fixed dark/light theme contrast across buttons, badges, banners, and video canvas.\n     - Cleaned out Google Meet OAuth environment variables from `.env.example`.\n     - Verified test suite (`npm test` passes 6/6 tests) and applet builds clean (`compile_applet`).\n   - **In Progress / Current Turn**:\n     - Read `/skills/system_skills/firebase-integration-rpc/SKILL.md` in full.\n     - Next mandatory step according to the Firebase Skill is initiating the Firebase provisioning flow via `show_aistudio_ui(ui_type: \"firebase_setup\")`.\n\n3. **Key Findings & Skill Directives**\n   - **Skill Constraint (MANDATORY)**: You MUST call `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type: \"firebase_setup\"`, then immediately **STOP THE CONVERSATION** and wait for the user to respond in the UI.\n   - **On Resume**: Call `rpc_action(service_name: \"fax\", method_name: \"GetFirebaseTos\")`. If and only if `\"accepted\": true`, call `rpc_action(service_name: \"fax\", method_name: \"ProvisionFirebase\", arguments: { platform: \"web\" })`.\n   - **Blueprint & Security Rules**:\n     - Create `firebase-blueprint.json` strictly modeling entities (`users`, `tracks`, `bookings`, `queue`, `feedbacks`, `ledger`, `admins`).\n     - Admin document: `admins/{uid}` where `deepanshu.chawla2608@gmail.com` UID is bootstrapped.\n     - Follow the Eight Pillars of Firestore Hardened Rules, generate `security_spec.md`, draft rules, run ESLint, and deploy via `rpc_action(service_name: \"fax\", method_name: \"DeployRules\")`.\n     - Catch Firestore errors using the structured `handleFirestoreError` format specified in the skill.\n\n4. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server running on port 3000 (`https://ais-dev-5qoxcmdkfdikkxzc7ht6yb-115831898357.asia-east1.run.app`).\n   - Current backend API is in `server.ts` with in-memory stores in `src/services/store.ts`.\n   - Frontend state is in `src/App.tsx`, `src/components/*`. Persona switching was previously mocked in `Navbar.tsx` and `App.tsx`.\n\n5. **Next Steps (Strict Order)**\n   1. **Trigger Firebase UI**: Call `show_aistudio_ui({ ui_type: \"firebase_setup\" })` and stop immediately.\n   2. **Verify ToS & Provision**: On resume, verify `GetFirebaseTos` is `accepted: true`, then call `ProvisionFirebase` with `platform: \"web\"`.\n   3. **Install Dependencies**: Install `firebase` package (`install_applet_package([\"firebase\"])`).\n   4. **Initialize Firebase SDK**: Wire `src/firebase.ts` reading `firebase-applet-config.json` and initialize Auth and Firestore (`export const db = getFirestore(app, firebaseConfig.firestoreDatabaseId)`).\n   5. **Create Auth & Data Layer**:\n     - Create `AuthContext.tsx` providing real Google login (`signInWithPopup`), logout, user profile state, and active role derivation.\n     - Bootstrap admin if `user.email === \'deepanshu.chawla2608@gmail.com\'`.\n     - Migrate `src/services/api.ts` to query Firestore collections with clean empty initial states (no dummy bookings, real dynamic tracks seeded once).\n     - Guard navigation tabs in `App.tsx` and `Navbar.tsx` based on `currentUser.roles` and `activeRole`.\n   6. **Rules & Deployment**:\n     - Create `firebase-blueprint.json` and `firestore.rules`.\n     - Deploy rules using `rpc_action({ service_name: \"fax\", method_name: \"DeployRules\" })`.\n   7. **Verify**: Run `compile_applet` and test with real sign-in and role isolation.\n\n6. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Do NOT attempt to hand-write Firebase configuration or mock auth. Use the standard AI Studio Firebase tools.\n   - Stop immediately after invoking `show_aistudio_ui(ui_type: \"firebase_setup\")`.\n   - Remove dummy/mock bookings so production users start with a clean slate.\n   - Restrict interviewer and admin routes strictly based on authentication and verified role authorization.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 291
    included_step_index_end: 335
    user_requests: "Instead of postgresql can you integrate mondodb , for can we integrate upi for payment method and for meet can we create inhouse solution instead of another 3rd party app and integrate light theme as well"
